<body><richtext>
<pardef id='1'/>
<par def='1'><run><font size='14pt' style='bold'/>Using Keep Design</run></par>
<par def='1'>1. Open Default-* elements in Domino Designer to see starter patterns.</par>
<par def='1'>2. Export or update via typed CRUD or bulk GET/PUT /designdxl.</par>
<par def='1'>3. Create new elements with POST/PUT; NSF defaults win over JAR fallbacks.</par>
<par def='1'>4. LotusScript libraries use Options, Declarations (classes), and one section per Function/Sub.</par>
<par def='1'>5. Java script libraries keep readable source; compiled .class may be stripped on git export (-ReadableJava).</par></richtext></body>
